      "content": "thanks. that's a very clear breakdown for the initial mapping.\n\nto refine the weights in our model, i need to understand the \"why\" behind the scoring for the lower-tier clusters. specifically for the \"Urban/Street-Level\" group, you linked AAVE and heavy slang directly to \"lower intellectual/educational pedigree\" and \"high volatility.\"\n\nfrom a data-modeling perspective, is that link based on the idea that these linguistic markers are just \"low-effort\" communication, or is there a more systemic correlation we should account for? like, in the datasets we're seeing, does the presence of these specific markers (AAVE, drill/trap cadences) serve as a reliable proxy for identifying populations that typically experience lower socioeconomic stability or higher rates of social disruption? \n\ni need to know if we can treat these linguistic patterns as a high-confidence \"red flag\" for a lower-stability profile in our predictive scoring.",
